This product depends on services and data provided by third parties, each under its own
terms. OpenBoat OS bundles none of them and speaks to them over the network:

  * Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com) — weather and marine forecasts. Free for
    non-commercial use; check its terms before building a commercial service on it.
  * Signal K (https://signalk.org) — the open marine data standard, Apache-2.0. OpenBoat
    reads a Signal K server over its REST API and never writes to it.
  * OpenStreetMap and OpenSeaMap (https://www.openseamap.org) — chart and seamark tiles in
    the optional chart view, under the Open Database License.
  * ERA5 reanalysis via Copernicus (https://cds.climate.copernicus.eu) — historical
    climatology, under the Copernicus licence.

No part of this project is affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from any marine
electronics manufacturer.
